-- title:
--   Drinfeld curve: q³+1 places fixed by (-1)-twisted Frobenius
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ and a field $k$ that is algebraically closed and carries an algebra structure over $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}=$ `GaloisField q 2`. Assume the coordinate ring `CoordRing q k`, the quotient of $k[X_0,X_1]$ by the ideal generated by `drinfeldPoly q k - 1`, is a domain, and that its fraction field `drinfeldFunctionField q k` is a curve over $k$ in the sense of [`AlgebraicCurve.IsCurveOver`](def/AlgebraicCurve_IsCurveOver.html#L15): divisors of nonzero functions exist and have degree $0$, every place has residue field finite over $k$, and the module of Kähler differentials over $k$ is free of rank one. Let $\varphi$ be a $k$-algebra endomorphism of this function field whose underlying ring map is integral and which sends the images of the coordinates `x q k` and `y q k` to their $q^2$-th powers. Let $\zeta$ be a $(q+1)$-st root of unity in $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$ whose underlying field element is $-1$, and let it act through the element of `hSubgroup q` (the kernel of `hChar q` inside $GL_2(\mathbb{Z}/q)\times\mathbb{F}_{q^2}^{\times}$) with trivial matrix component and unit component $\zeta$, via `hFunctionFieldAction q k`, which extends the automorphism of `CoordRing q k` given by `hAction q k` to the fraction field. The assertion is that the set of places $w$ of the function field over $k$ — valuation subrings containing $k$, proper, and principal ideal rings — whose pullback [`AlgebraicCurve.Place.restrictAlong φ hφi w`](def/AlgebraicCurve_Correspondence.html#L204) (the comap of $w$'s valuation subring along $\varphi$) equals the translate of $w$ by that automorphism is finite of cardinality $q^3+1$.
--
--   This is the point count over $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$ of the $(-1)$-twisted form of the Drinfeld curve $xy^q-x^qy=1$, a Hermitian, hence $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$-maximal, curve: $q^3+1=q^2+1+2gq$ with $g=q(q-1)/2$. It feeds the trace computation [`DrinfeldCurve.cast_mul_trace_eq_natCard_restrictAlong_eq_smul_sub`](thm.html#DrinfeldCurve.cast_mul_trace_eq_natCard_restrictAlong_eq_smul_sub), where fixed-point counts of twisted Frobenius are matched with traces on cohomology.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_DrinfeldCurve_natCard_place_restrictAlong_eq_neg_one_smul.lean

